            question: "A newborn fails to pass meconium within the first 48 hours. He develops abdominal distension and bilious vomiting. A rectal suction biopsy is performed to confirm the diagnosis. To definitively diagnose this disease, the biopsy must prove the absence of ganglion cells in which layer(s) of the bowel?",
