            question: "A 25-year-old female presents with chronic, bloody diarrhea and left lower quadrant abdominal pain. Colonoscopy reveals continuous inflammation starting at the rectum and extending proximally to the splenic flexure. The mucosa is highly friable with pseudopolyps. Which histological feature is the hallmark of this disease?",
