            topic: "Female Genital System", difficulty: "Normal", source: "Pathoma",
            question: "A 30-year-old female has a routine Pap smear showing high-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion (HSIL). High-risk HPV (strains 16 and 18) is detected. The oncogenic potential of these viruses is primarily due to viral proteins E6 and E7. What are their specific respective targets?",
