            exp: "A Complete Hydatidiform Mole occurs when an empty egg is fertilized by a sperm that duplicates its DNA (46,XX, entirely paternal). Because maternal DNA is absent, p57 (a paternally imprinted, maternally expressed gene) is negative. A partial mole has fetal parts, is 69,XXY, and is p57 positive.",
