            topic: "General Pathology", difficulty: "Normal", source: "Robbins",
            question: "A 65-year-old patient with long-standing rheumatoid arthritis develops nephrotic syndrome, restrictive cardiomyopathy, and an enlarged tongue (macroglossia). Tissue biopsy stained with Congo red shows apple-green birefringence under polarized light. What is the precursor protein for the amyloid depositing in this patient?",
