            topic: "Gastrointestinal", difficulty: "Normal", source: "Pathoma",
            question: "An elderly male presents with dysphagia, halitosis (bad breath), and the feeling of a lump in his neck. He occasionally regurgitates undigested food he ate days ago. This condition is caused by a herniation of the pharyngeal mucosa through an area of muscular weakness. What is this specific area called?",
