            exp: "Primary Sclerosing Cholangitis (PSC) involves inflammation and fibrosis of both intra- and extrahepatic bile ducts. The classic findings are 'onion-skin' periductal fibrosis on biopsy and a 'beaded' appearance on ERCP. It is strongly associated with Ulcerative Colitis and p-ANCA positivity.",
