            exp: "In severe acute pancreatitis, lipase digests peripancreatic fat, releasing free fatty acids. These fatty acids bind with serum calcium to form chalky white salts—a process called saponification (fat necrosis). Severe hypocalcemia indicates massive fat necrosis and is a classic marker of a very poor prognosis.",
