            exp: "Hepatic angiosarcoma is a rare, highly malignant tumor of endothelial cells (hence CD31 positive). It is a classic board question heavily associated with exposure to Vinyl chloride (used in making PVC plastics), Arsenic, and Thorotrast (an old radiocontrast dye).",
