            exp: "Chronic pancreatitis is most commonly caused by chronic alcohol abuse (in adults) or Cystic Fibrosis (in children). It leads to irreversible fibrosis and calcification. Destruction of the exocrine pancreas causes malabsorption/steatorrhea, and destruction of the endocrine islets leads to secondary Diabetes Mellitus.",
