            question: "A patient presents with nephrotic and nephritic features. Renal biopsy reveals a 'tram-track' appearance of the GBM on silver stain. Immunofluorescence shows subendothelial deposits of IgG and C3. This specific pathology (Membranoproliferative Glomerulonephritis Type I) is most strongly associated with chronic infection by which pathogen?",
