            topic: "Renal Pathology", difficulty: "Hard", source: "Kaplan",
            question: "A 45-year-old male is treated with a course of Ampicillin. One week later, he develops a fever, an erythematous maculopapular rash, and flank pain. Urinalysis reveals white blood cell casts containing a high percentage of eosinophils. This Acute Interstitial Nephritis (AIN) is primarily mediated by which type of hypersensitivity reaction?",
            options: ["Type I only", "Type II only", "Type III only", "Type I and Type IV"],
            correct: 3,
            exp: "Acute Interstitial Nephritis is a drug-induced hypersensitivity reaction of the renal interstitium. It acts via a combination of Type I (IgE-mediated, leading to eosinophil recruitment) and Type IV (T-cell mediated delayed hypersensitivity) reactions.",
