            correct: 2,
            exp: "Renal Papillary Necrosis classically presents with gross hematuria and flank pain. It is triggered by conditions that cause ischemia in the renal medulla. The classic triggers are summarized by 'SAAD papa': Sickle cell disease/trait, Analgesics (NSAIDs), Acute pyelonephritis, and Diabetes mellitus.",
            book: "Pathoma: Fundamentals of Pathology", subtopic: "Tubulointerstitial Diseases"
