            question: "A fetus is noted to have a severe lack of amniotic fluid (oligohydramnios) on ultrasound. After birth, the infant has a flattened face, low-set ears, and clubfeet, and rapidly dies of pulmonary hypoplasia. This 'Potter sequence' is most commonly caused by which congenital renal anomaly?",
            options: ["Horseshoe kidney", "Bilateral renal agenesis", "Unilateral renal agenesis", "Pelvic kidney"],
            correct: 1,
            exp: "Potter sequence is caused by severe oligohydramnios. Because amniotic fluid is primarily composed of fetal urine, Bilateral Renal Agenesis means no urine is produced. The lack of fluid causes physical compression of the fetus (flat face, clubfeet) and prevents normal lung development, leading to fatal pulmonary hypoplasia.",
