            options: ["Superior mesenteric artery", "Inferior mesenteric artery", "Celiac trunk", "Renal artery"],
            correct: 1,
            exp: "A horseshoe kidney occurs when the lower poles of the two kidneys fuse during development. As they attempt to ascend from the pelvis into the abdomen, they get caught on the root of the Inferior Mesenteric Artery (IMA) and remain abnormally low in the abdomen.",
