            correct: 2,
            exp: "Type 2 (Proximal) RTA is caused by a defect in bicarbonate reabsorption in the PCT. Because bicarbonate is lost in the urine, the blood becomes acidotic. Eventually, the filtered load of bicarbonate drops so low that the distal tubule can resorb what is left, so the urine can eventually be acidified. It is often seen as part of Fanconi syndrome.",
