            question: "A 60-year-old male undergoes a radical nephrectomy for a large, yellowish renal mass. The pathologist notes that the tumor has invaded into the renal vein. This specific path of invasion makes the tumor highly prone to metastasizing to which organ?",
            options: ["Brain", "Lungs", "Contralateral kidney", "Liver"],
            correct: 1,
            exp: "Renal Cell Carcinoma famously loves to invade the renal vein, sometimes growing as a continuous solid column of tumor up the Inferior Vena Cava and even into the right side of the heart. Because it enters the systemic venous circulation directly, its most common site of metastasis is the lungs.",
