            exp: "The normal bladder is lined by transitional epithelium (urothelium). In response to chronic irritation (e.g., chronic cystitis, kidney stones, Schistosoma infection), the urothelium undergoes squamous metaplasia (changing to a tougher squamous epithelium). If the irritation persists, this metaplasia can progress to dysplasia and eventually Squamous Cell Carcinoma.",
