            question: "A 40-year-old female who successfully underwent chemotherapy for breast cancer 5 years ago presents with severe, progressive biventricular heart failure. Echocardiogram shows all four chambers are massively dilated. Which chemotherapeutic agent is notoriously cardiotoxic and likely caused this irreversible Dilated Cardiomyopathy?",
            options: ["Cyclophosphamide", "Doxorubicin (Adriamycin)", "Cisplatin", "Vincristine"],
