            exp: "Staphylococcus epidermidis is the absolute most common cause of early Prosthetic Valve Endocarditis. It is normally a harmless skin commensal, but it is highly adept at infecting foreign medical devices (valves, catheters) by secreting a thick, extracellular polysaccharide biofilm that protects it from antibiotics and immune cells.",
