            exp: "This is an acute rupture of the Posteromedial Papillary Muscle, leading to massive, acute mitral regurgitation (holosystolic murmur at the apex) and catastrophic pulmonary edema. The posteromedial papillary muscle is especially vulnerable because it typically has only a single blood supply from the Posterior Descending Artery (PDA).",
