            exp: "Dipyridamole (and Adenosine) are powerful vasodilators. In a heart with atherosclerosis, the vessels distal to the plaque are already maximally dilated at rest to maintain flow. When Dipyridamole dilates all the healthy vessels, blood takes the path of least resistance, 'stealing' flow away from the ischemic areas and triggering angina.",
