            question: "A 35-year-old female presents with fever, confusion, and petechiae. Labs show severe thrombocytopenia, elevated LDH, and a normal PT and PTT. Peripheral smear demonstrates numerous schistocytes. What is the specific molecular pathogenesis of this life-threatening syndrome?",
