            question: "A 55-year-old male presents with massive splenomegaly and extreme fatigue. His white blood cell count is 150,000/uL with a full spectrum of granulocytic cells (from myeloblasts to mature neutrophils). The Leukocyte Alkaline Phosphatase (LAP) score is completely zero. Which targeted therapy is the definitive first-line treatment for his disease?",
