            question: "A 60-year-old male with severe liver cirrhosis presents with vomiting of bright red blood. He has dilated veins around his umbilicus and an enlarged spleen. The hematemesis is most likely due to the rupture of varices located in the lower esophagus. These varices are formed by an anastomosis between the systemic azygos vein and which portal system vein?",
