            question: "A 5-year-old boy presents with severe swelling and pain in his right knee (hemarthrosis) after a minor fall. Labs show a significantly prolonged PTT, a normal PT, and a normal bleeding time. Mixing the patient's plasma with normal plasma corrects the PTT. What is the most likely diagnosis?",
