            question: "A fetus from Southeast Asian parents is found to have massive generalized edema, pleural effusions, and ascites (Hydrops fetalis) on ultrasound, and dies in utero. The cause is determined to be the complete deletion of all four alpha-globin genes. The predominant hemoglobin found in this fetus (Hb Barts) is a tetramer of which globin chain?",
