            exp: "Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia (CLL) is the most common adult leukemia. It involves a proliferation of naive B cells that co-express CD5 and CD20. These neoplastic cells are structurally fragile and routinely rupture when spread on a glass slide, forming classic 'smudge cells'.",
