            correct: 1,
            exp: "The two most common causes of acute pancreatitis are alcohol abuse and gallstones. A gallstone can travel down the common bile duct and become lodged at the Ampulla of Vater. This blocks the main pancreatic duct as well, causing pancreatic enzymes to back up and prematurely activate, leading to autodigestion.",
