            options: ["Protein C", "Tissue Factor Pathway Inhibitor (TFPI)", "Plasminogen", "Antithrombin III"],
            correct: 3,
            exp: "Heparin works by binding to Antithrombin III and inducing a conformational change that increases its activity by up to 1000-fold. Activated Antithrombin III then rapidly inactivates Thrombin (Factor IIa) and Factor Xa, halting the coagulation cascade.",
            book: "Kaplan Medical USMLE Step 1 Pathology", subtopic: "Coagulation Pharmacology"
