            exp: "To diagnose Hirschsprung disease, the biopsy must demonstrate an absence of ganglion cells. The Meissner plexus is in the submucosa, but the Auerbach (myenteric) plexus is located deep within the Muscularis Propria (between the inner circular and outer longitudinal muscle layers). A full-thickness biopsy is needed to sample this layer.",
