            question: "A 50-year-old male presents with blistering skin lesions on the sun-exposed areas of his hands and face. He has a history of Hepatitis C and alcohol abuse. His urine turns a dark, 'tea-color' upon standing in sunlight. This acquired porphyria is caused by a defect in which enzyme?",
