            question: "A patient with suspected von Willebrand Disease (vWD) undergoes platelet aggregation studies. The addition of Ristocetin fails to induce aggregation. However, when NORMAL plasma is added to the patient's sample along with Ristocetin, platelet aggregation proceeds perfectly. This specific correction proves that the defect lies in the:",
