            exp: "Acute bacterial sialadenitis typically occurs in elderly or post-operative patients who become dehydrated (leading to decreased salivary flow and stasis). The stagnant saliva becomes an excellent culture medium for ascending bacteria from the oral cavity, overwhelmingly Staphylococcus aureus.",
