            question: "An infant is diagnosed with an exocrine pancreatic anomaly. During embryogenesis, the pancreas forms from a dorsal bud and a ventral bud that must rotate and fuse. If they fail to fuse, the bulk of the pancreas is forced to drain through the tiny accessory duct of Santorini instead of the main duct of Wirsung. What is this congenital defect called?",
            options: ["Annular pancreas", "Pancreas divisum", "Heterotopic pancreas", "Biliary atresia"],
