            question: "A 65-year-old female presents with recurrent bouts of acute pancreatitis. An ERCP reveals a massively dilated main pancreatic duct. Endoscopy shows thick, viscous mucin extruding directly out of the Ampulla of Vater. The tumor is found to lack ovarian-type stroma. What is the diagnosis?",
