            exp: "Intraductal Papillary Mucinous Neoplasms (IPMNs) arise within the main pancreatic duct (or its major branches). They secrete massive amounts of mucin, which severely dilates the duct and can be seen oozing from the Ampulla. Unlike MCNs, they occur more often in men, involve the main duct, and lack ovarian-type stroma.",
