            question: "A 60-year-old male is diagnosed with a rare Acinar Cell Carcinoma of the pancreas. He presents with a bizarre constellation of symptoms: widespread subcutaneous fat necrosis (causing painful skin nodules) and severe polyarthralgias. The tumor is causing this syndrome by massively overproducing which exocrine enzyme into the bloodstream?",
