            question: "A 55-year-old female undergoes a CT scan for an unrelated issue. An incidental, 3 cm cystic mass is found in the tail of her pancreas. Biopsy of the cyst wall reveals it is lined by cuboidal cells and backed by a dense, spindle-cell stroma that looks identical to ovarian tissue. What is this premalignant lesion?",
