            exp: "Acute Respiratory Distress Syndrome (ARDS) is a highly lethal complication of severe acute pancreatitis. The massive systemic release of pancreatic enzymes (especially phospholipase and proteases) damages the alveolar-capillary interface in the lungs and destroys pulmonary surfactant, leading to non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema.",
