            topic: "Exocrine Pathology", difficulty: "Hard", source: "Robbins",
            question: "A 60-year-old male with long-standing chronic alcoholic pancreatitis presents with malabsorption and severe weight loss. His physician orders a serum amylase and lipase. The results come back completely normal. Why are these marker enzymes not elevated despite his severe, ongoing pancreatic disease?",
