            exp: "The PanIN progression model follows a highly predictable genetic sequence. Telomere shortening happens first, followed by early activating mutations in the KRAS oncogene. As the dysplasia worsens (PanIN-2), the p16 (CDKN2A) tumor suppressor is inactivated. Finally, the inactivation of p53 and SMAD4 drives the jump to invasive adenocarcinoma.",
