            correct: 1,
            exp: "Hypercalcemia (from hyperparathyroidism, myeloma, etc.) is a well-known cause of acute pancreatitis. High intracellular calcium levels directly trigger the premature, aberrant activation of trypsinogen into active trypsin while it is still inside the pancreatic acinar cells, setting off the autodigestion cascade.",
            book: "Kaplan Medical USMLE Step 1 Pathology", subtopic: "Exocrine Pancreas"
