            question: "A 30-year-old female presents with well-demarcated, salmon-colored plaques covered with silvery scales on her elbows and knees. When she scrapes off a scale, pinpoint bleeding occurs. What is the histological term for the retention of nuclei in the stratum corneum that causes this scaling?",
