            exp: "Xeroderma Pigmentosum is caused by a profound defect in Nucleotide Excision Repair (NER). UV light causes adjacent pyrimidines (thymines) in DNA to covalently bond, forming thymine dimers. Normally, NER cuts these out and replaces them. Without NER, mutations accumulate rapidly, leading to extreme photosensitivity and early, lethal skin cancers.",
