            question: "A 6-month-old infant presents with intensely pruritic, erythematous, oozing, and crusted lesions on his cheeks and scalp. The mother notes the infant constantly rubs his face against the crib sheets. The child also has a strong family history of asthma and allergic rhinitis. What is the fundamental histological hallmark of this eczematous dermatitis?",
