            exp: "Tuberous Sclerosis is an autosomal dominant neurocutaneous syndrome. The classic facial rash consists of bilateral, reddish-brown papules across the nose and cheeks called Angiofibromas (historically and incorrectly termed 'adenoma sebaceum'). Patients also get ash-leaf spots, shagreen patches, and periungual fibromas.",
            book: "Pathoma: Fundamentals of Pathology", subtopic: "Neurocutaneous Syndromes"
