            correct: 2,
            exp: "A Port-Wine Stain (Nevus flammeus) in the distribution of the trigeminal nerve is the cardinal sign of Sturge-Weber syndrome. This is a non-inherited developmental anomaly characterized by capillary malformations on the face and ipsilateral leptomeningeal angiomas in the brain, leading to severe seizures, intellectual disability, and early-onset glaucoma.",
