            question: "A 22-year-old child from a poverty-stricken area presents with severe edema, a swollen abdomen, and reddish, depigmented hair. He has profound protein malnutrition (Kwashiorkor). If a pancreatic biopsy were taken, what adaptive change would be overwhelmingly seen in his exocrine acinar cells?",
            options: ["Hypertrophy", "Metaplasia", "Atrophy", "Dysplasia"],
